# AnemiaScan V3.1 model weights (~150MB; base_models/convnext_tiny_best.pth
# alone is 111MB, over GitHub's 100MB hard file limit). Never commit these.
#
# This used to ignore the whole `app/ml/model_assets/` directory, which also
# swallowed the small JSON configs and BUNDLE_README.md — including the very
# README the line below tells you to read. A fresh clone therefore got an empty
# directory and no way to find out what belonged in it. Only the binaries are
# ignored now; runtime_config.json, thresholds.json, calibration.json,
# inference_contract.json and BUNDLE_README.md are tracked, so the operating
# threshold, the calibration parameters and the inference contract are
# reviewable without possessing the weights.
#
# The weights themselves are obtained separately and MUST be verified against
# the SHA-256 digests recorded in ../MODEL_CARD.md before use: the on-chain
# modelHash is keccak256 of that manifest (app/ml/manifest.py), so a substituted
# or truncated checkpoint silently changes the model's identity and every
# commitment anchored under it. `python -m app.ml.manifest` prints the digests
# of whatever is actually installed — compare, don't assume.
app/ml/model_assets/**/*.pth
app/ml/model_assets/**/*.joblib
app/ml/model_assets/**/*.npz
